{"corpus":"ccc","number":757,"text_html":"<span>« L’Église<sup class=\"srcRef cccRef\">§507</sup> s’appelle encore « la Jérusalem d’en haut » et « notre mère » <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"1\">1</sup> ; elle est décrite comme l’épouse immaculée de l’Agneau immaculé <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"3\">2</sup> que le Christ ‘a aimée, pour laquelle il s’est livré afin de la sanctifier<sup class=\"srcRef cccRef\">§796</sup><sup class=\"srcRef cccRef\">§1616</sup>’ <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"7\">3</sup>, qu’il s’est associée par un pacte indissoluble, qu’il ne cesse de ‘nourrir et d’entourer de soins’ <sup class=\"srcRef bibleRef\" data-idx=\"8\">4</sup> » <sup class=\"srcRef docRef\" data-idx=\"a\">a</sup>.</span>","cross_refs":["507","796","1616"],"bible_refs":[{"text":"Ga 4:26"},{"text":"Ap 12:17"},{"text":"Ap 19:7"},{"text":"Ap 21:2"},{"text":"Ap 21:9"},{"text":"Ap 22:17"},{"text":"Ep 5:26"},{"text":"Ep 5:29"}],"citations":[],"magisterial_refs":[{"type":"bible","raw":"Ga 4:26","idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible","raw":"voir Ap 12:17","idx":2,"marker_idx":1,"display_idx":1},{"type":"bible","raw":"voir Ap 19:7","idx":3,"display_idx":2},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"21:2","idx":4,"marker_idx":3,"display_idx":2},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"21:9","idx":5,"marker_idx":3,"display_idx":2},{"type":"bible_continuation","raw":"22:17","idx":6,"marker_idx":3,"display_idx":2},{"type":"bible","raw":"Ep 5:26","idx":7,"display_idx":3},{"type":"bible","raw":"Ep 5:29","idx":8,"display_idx":4},{"type":"magisterial","raw":"LG 6","idx":"a","doc_raw":"LG 6"}]}